      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. like you said, they're looking for \"stable, undisturbed data points.\" it's not just about noise, it's about the baseline. if they do it during the day, the traffic vibration masks everything else. but at 2am, the only vibration is us walking around in our houses. i also noticed the crew on Thursday was using a device that looked like a seismic monitor, not a plumber's tool. if they're trying to build a map of the neighborhood's internal movement, what kind of tech would they actually be using to transmit that data without being detected?",
